; A discriminated form with no discriminant supplied. `:kind` selects which
; `(variant …)` applies, so without it the validator cannot know which key
; set to check `(track)` against — it reports the missing discriminant
; rather than guessing a variant or falling through to the common keys.
;
; `:kind` carries no `:default` here, deliberately. The corpus reaches this
; code today only through `effective-axis-d-*`, where the key DOES default
; and the case exists to show axis D suppressing the diagnostic. That makes
; the axis-off baseline incidental to those cases; this one pins the plain
; reading directly, on a form where no overlay could apply.
(plugin :name probe :version "1.0.0"
  (value-kind :name kind-tag
    :underlying symbol
    :members (member-set :values [kick bass]))
  (form :name track
    :discriminant kind
    (key :name kind :type kind-tag :optional true)
    (variant :when kick
      (key :name step :type number :optional true))
    (variant :when bass
      (key :name sequence :type any :optional true))))

(track)
